WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:04.790
Here's an empty times-table
grid: 10 rows by 10 columns.

2
00:00:04.840 --> 00:00:09.210
Press run, and it fills itself
in, one answer after another,

3
00:00:09.260 --> 00:00:11.270
all 100 of them.

4
00:00:11.320 --> 00:00:13.270
Now look at the program behind it.

5
00:00:13.320 --> 00:00:15.230
It's only a few lines long.

6
00:00:15.280 --> 00:00:17.990
Are 100 output lines hidden somewhere?

7
00:00:18.040 --> 00:00:20.850
Or is one line copied over and over?

8
00:00:20.900 --> 00:00:24.610
So how can so few lines print 100 answers?

9
00:00:24.660 --> 00:00:29.230
In this mission, you'll see sequence:
statements run one after another,

10
00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:31.290
in order, top to bottom.

11
00:00:31.340 --> 00:00:35.530
Then you'll make a block of code repeat,
with a counter that goes up by 1 each

12
00:00:35.580 --> 00:00:36.830
time round.

13
00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:42.640
Your mission: explain how a few lines of
code can print all 100 times-table answers.
